SWEET MALI interrupts (patch 0157, plan oneshot-2 step G4, docs/research/35 s.8): boot-arg sweetmali bit 0x200 (with 1|2 or 0x100) takes the Mali JOB
and MMU interrupts (INTID 452/453 = SPI 420/421, stock oriole DT; GPU INTID 451 is never attached) instead of the 200 us poll.
- pexpert/arm/sweet_spi.h (pure, shim/sweet_spi_host_test.c): allowlist 452/453, GICD offsets, attach preconditions, IRQ dispatch decision.
- pe_fiq.c: sweet_spi_attach/detach + sweet_spi_irq. Attach READS ICFGR/IGRPMODR/IROUTER (must be level / 0 / this CPU, as the 0109 probe read
  them) and writes only ICENABLER, ICPENDR, ICACTIVER, IGROUPR |= bit, ISENABLER (bounded RWP waits), then reads back; not sticking = detach.
- sleh.c: SPIs go to sweet_spi_irq first. Once any SPI is attached the net is armed: an SPI without a handler is masked (ICENABLER) and counted
  instead of being EOId and re-taken forever (review M2). Before the first attach nothing changes.
- sweet_mali.c: ISR reads *_IRQ_STATUS, writes that *_IRQ_MASK to 0, counts, wakes sm_thread; masks armed at submit (slot done/fail bits,
  MMU AS0 page fault + bus error), zeroed in finish(); sm_thread keeps check_job and its timeouts, fallback deadline 5 ms; dead = GIC detach
  then masks 0; review 0155 F1: a replay submit failure other than EINVAL leaks the BOs (a job may run); counts printed: "SWEET MALI: irq counts mode=... job=N mmu=N spurious=N unhandled_spi=N". Without bit 0x200 nothing changes.

